# Resolves an already-evaluated instance-expression reference to the STATIC method reference.
# The caller passes the live reference (e.g. instRef.[pExpr], $cando already checked).
# Distinguishes a method hiding in an $obj from a plain class method, then climbs the class
# superclass chain — $methods.$findname finds NO inherited methods, so we must walk up.
# @? a method in a SUPERclass of the $obj is not yet handled (pragmatic: only the direct $obj)

If pExprRef.$obj().$class ## method hides in an $obj on the window
	Quit method pExprRef.$obj().$methods.$findname(pExprRef.$name).$ref
End If

# plain class method → climb the superclass chain
Calculate methodname as pExprRef.$name
Set reference classRef to pExprRef.$class().$ref
Repeat
	Set reference methodRef to classRef.$methods.$findname(methodname)
	If methodRef.$class
		Quit method methodRef
	End If
	Set reference classRef to $cinst.$superclassRef(classRef)
Until isclear(classRef)

Quit method methodRef ## empty if not found